      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JILLIBY BLISS (7) had been racing in great heart then went close again last time over 1800m at Globe Derby Park, finishing second and just a nose from the winner. Should enjoy a nice smother from this draw and will be looking for a split at some stage. Meets a similar line up and she can figure in the finish. EAGLESTONE (2) has been in the money three times from as many runs this prep and went close again last start over 2230m at Globe Derby Park, finishing third and 20 metres from the winner. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Finds a nice race and can grab a well-deserved win. HELPISFARAWAY (1) broke last start and finished a distant last over 2070m at this track when resuming. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Only needs to get things right to be in the money. EMILY MEAGAN (6) is better than her last-start eighth over 1690m at Kilmore would suggest. Well worth a second look.",
